WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.801
♪♪

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.968
-The [bleep] is you
supposed to be?

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:06.000
-Hi. I'm Stede.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.634
-He's the Gentleman Pirate.

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:12.567
-Well, I got bad news for you,
genital pirate.

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:15.067
I'm about to start
a whole new nose jar.

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:19.868
-Uh, baby?
-Don't say that.

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:21.200
Don't call me that.
-Well, I just figured,

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.367
since we're married --
-None of my other husbands

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:24.868
have a problem with this.
-That's mine.

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:26.534
-Do not call me that in here.

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:28.334
-Okay. Well, you see,
Hans was in here

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:31.200
asking about him for his boss.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.400
-Blackbeard?

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.634
Mother [bleep] Blackbeard
want to talk to this guy?

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:38.567
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
That was a clip

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:41.701
from the new comedy series
"Our Flag Means Death."

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:43.634
We're here talking
to Leslie Jones.

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:46.000
And are you enjoying
playing a pirate?

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.934
-Yes!
Are you kidding me?!

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:50.834
That's like giving candy
to a baby.

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:52.968
Are you serious?

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:55.934
First of all, they had me
a pirate and wooden hand,

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:58.901
and then they added on
I have 19 husbands.

00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:02.033
What?
That is like my dream.

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:03.467
Hello!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:05.167
I just -- It was --
It was so --

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:07.300
And the director
was so good.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.667
Like, for real, Seth.
Like, he pulled it out of me.

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:13.133
Like -- Like, you see --
You've never seen me that calm.

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:14.767
-No, that's true.
-You've never seen me that calm.

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:17.367
And I, like --
You know what he told me?

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:18.868
Which I love.
Him and David --

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:20.868
David Jenkins came up to me,
and they was just like,

00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:23.267
"We are so excited
to have Leslie Jones here,

00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:25.033
but we don't want
Leslie Jones on the screen.

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:26.534
We want Spanish Jackie."

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:28.701
And it was so fun for --

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.567
Ignacio would tell me,
he was like,

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:32.267
"You're Spanish Jackie.
Nobody --

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:34.467
You don't go to anyone.
Someone comes to you."

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:36.000
Like, it was so --

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.734
The direction was so good.
It was so good.

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:40.667
-And it's really fun.
There we see that Fred Armisen

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.334
is one of your 19 husbands.

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:44.767
It must've been fun
to work with Fred, as well.

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:46.400
-You know how crazy
Fred is, right?

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.501
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Fred is so good

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:50.567
at what he does,
and he's so quick.

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:54.634
So we immediately
became like a real couple.

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:56.400
And, like -- we --
Like, it was like --

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.734
'Cause Fred was like
one of my favorite husbands.

00:01:58.734 --> 00:02:00.634
He's around.
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:02.534
And he lets me do crazy stuff.

00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:04.033
He lets me hurt him
and all of that.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:06.234
Like, yeah.
He's my favorite husband.

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:08.167
Like, but I'm not gonna
let him know that.

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:12.267
And it's me and Fred just --
We're like -- I love him.

00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:13.634
I love people who are quick.

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:14.701
Like you!
I love you.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.267
That's why I love
interviewing with you.

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:17.767
'Cause you so quick.
-Yeah, but you love me,

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:20.133
and I can't even get one
of the 19 husband roles.

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:21.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:24.133
Um, Seth, you are
gonna be president soon,

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:26.200
and you do not want the scandal
of being with me.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.200
-Very kind of you to say.
Hey, um, I want --

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.267
We always talk about TV shows
you're enthusiastic about.

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:35.167
We have long been looking
for our next "Game of Thrones"

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:37.434
that we could watch together.
What are you watching right now?

00:02:37.434 --> 00:02:39.734
Oh, my God!
Okay. So I'm watching "Bel Air."

00:02:39.734 --> 00:02:41.067
You know the new "Bel Air"?
-Yeah.

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:42.667
-Oh, my gosh, Seth!
It's so good!

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:44.868
-Great.
-It's so good!

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:47.901
-"Station 11."
-"Station 11" -- great.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.534
-So good!
So good. Okay?

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:51.968
So good.
Okay.

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:53.701
Make sure that you watch
"Legendary."

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:56.968
"Legendary" is on HBO Max, too.
-Okay.

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:58.467
-Of course, you know,
"Euphoria."

00:02:58.467 --> 00:03:01.701
"Euphoria" is the worst version
of Charlie Brown I ever seen.

00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:04.067
[ Laughter ]
Like, it's like --

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:05.467
Like, it's like --

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:07.834
Wait, no, we need
the "wah wah wah" in this.

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:10.267
Like, good God!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:12.601
It's --
I'm watching so many things.

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:15.067
I --
I'm just, like, tickled

00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:16.434
with some of the stuff
that's coming out

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:18.234
because it's so good.
"Bel Air" -- so good.

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:22.601
Are you watching some adaptation
of "Anne of Green Gables"?

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:25.534
-What?
There's a -- What?

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:26.701
Wait a minute.
'Cause I love

00:03:26.701 --> 00:03:28.133
"Anne of Green Gables" now.

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:30.467
I watched the new one.
There's another one?

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:32.400
-No, no, that's the one
I'm talking about.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.934
Oh, is that the best show?

00:03:34.934 --> 00:03:36.434
-I don't know.
I'm not watching it.

00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:37.567
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:03:37.567 --> 00:03:39.968
Then why did you ask me
about it, then?

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:42.100
Because I heard
that you had watched it,

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.434
and you're the guest.

00:03:43.434 --> 00:03:46.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:48.801
-No, "Anne of Green Gables,"
like, it's kind of --

00:03:48.801 --> 00:03:50.200
You know, I've already seen it.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.734
I mean, I'm pretty sure
everyone --

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:52.834
I don't know
why you brought that up,

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:54.467
but, yeah,
we could talk about it.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:55.901
Like, it's really good.

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:58.501
It's a very good remake
of the original.

00:03:58.501 --> 00:03:59.934
-Okay.
-"Anne of Green Gables."

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:02.167
That girl is so perfect
for that role.

00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:03.267
I love her.
-All right, great.

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:04.601
So which one should
we watch together?

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:07.567
'Cause I haven't seen --
What --

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:09.801
I mean, I feel like "Euphoria"
would be fun to watch together.

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:11.868
Should we do that?

00:04:11.868 --> 00:04:14.767
-Oh, my God.
Have you watched it, Seth?

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:16.734
-I haven't watched a lot of it.

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:19.567
-Oh, Seth, that's the new
"Game of Thrones" for us.

00:04:19.567 --> 00:04:20.701
-Yeah.
-That's it.

00:04:20.701 --> 00:04:22.667
-Yes, that's it.
Oh, my God!

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:25.000
-I feel like it's like...

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.834
a real life "Game of Thrones"
and how shocking it is.

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:31.267
-Dude, I...
That is --

00:04:31.267 --> 00:04:33.167
That is the best idea.

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:34.934
But, look, we got to start
from season one, though.

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:38.167
-Great.
-Oh, my God.

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:40.701
That makes me excited.
You know I'm crazy.

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:42.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.467
And you gotta love
yelling at the TV.

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:45.767
-I mean, this is --
I feel like this

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:47.167
would be really fun.
So here's the deal.

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.267
The next time you come out here,
we'll do, like, a test run.

00:04:49.267 --> 00:04:51.434
We'll do a pilot of --
-Let's do a couple of them

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:53.033
since we gonna do season one
'cause we got to do a wrap --

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.667
-Yeah.
-Oh, my God!

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:56.267
That sounds so good!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.267 --> 00:04:58.400
-All right. Here we go.
We figured it out together.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.367
Hey, Leslie, as always,

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:02.067
I love seeing you.
I love you very much.

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:03.701
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.868
-Thank you, baby.
You know, I miss you so much.

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:07.767
-I miss you, too.
I'm gonna get you out here.

00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:09.200
Leslie Jones, everybody!

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.467
"Our Flag Means Death"
streams on HBO Max

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:12.968
with new episodes
every Thursday.

